# Comments & Error Resolution

## Comment philosophy

Code should be **self-documenting** first. Comments explain **why**, not **what**.

### Write a comment when

- Business rules are non-obvious (maker-checker, MFA gates, idempotency guards).
- A workaround exists for a library bug or backend quirk — include issue/link.
- An algorithm or financial calculation needs justification.
- Public utility/hook has non-obvious constraints — use JSDoc.

### Do not comment when

- The code already reads clearly (`// increment counter` above `count++`).
- Restating the function name or prop name.
- Leaving commented-out code "for later" — delete it; git has history.

## Comment style

```typescript
// Single-line: sentence case, no period for fragments.

/**
 * Multi-line JSDoc for exported hooks, utilities, and complex functions.
 * @param scope - Permission scope from membership (e.g. 'approve_financing')
 */
```

- Use **English** for all comments (codebase language is English; UI strings are Persian).
- Keep comments **short** — one or two lines max inline; expand only in JSDoc when needed.
- Group related constants with a single block comment, not per-line noise.

## Resolving non-TypeScript errors

### ESLint

- Fix the violation; do not disable the rule unless team-approved and documented inline.
- Run `yarn lint` after every implementation.
- Common fixes: unused vars (remove), missing deps in `useEffect` (add or justify), import order.

### Build errors (Next.js)

- **Module not found** — fix import path or add missing dependency.
- **Server/client boundary** — move hook usage to a client component; add `'use client'`.
- **Metadata / static export** — ensure server-only APIs are not imported in client bundles.

### Runtime errors

- Reproduce in dev, fix root cause, add a guard or error boundary where appropriate.
- API errors: handle in Ky client + TanStack Query `onError`; show user-facing Persian message.

### Test failures (when tests exist)

- Fix implementation or update test if requirements changed — never delete tests to green the build.

## Error boundaries

- Use `error.tsx` at route segments for recoverable page-level failures.
- Feature-critical flows (payment, approval) should show actionable retry UI, not a blank screen.

## Checklist before marking work complete

```
[ ] No TypeScript errors in changed files
[ ] yarn lint passes
[ ] yarn build passes (if in scope)
[ ] No unjustified @ts-ignore / eslint-disable
[ ] No commented-out code blocks
[ ] Comments only where WHY is non-obvious
[ ] Manual smoke test of affected UI
```
